  "Question": "A farmer bought \\(749\\) sheep. He sold \\(700\\) of them for the price paid for the \\(749\\) sheep. The remaining \\(49\\) sheep were sold at the same price per head as the other \\(700.\\) Based on the cost, the percent gain on the entire transaction is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6.5\\)",
    "B": "\\(6.75\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(7.5\\)",
    "E": "\\(8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The first \\(700\\) sheep recover the entire purchase cost, so the money received for the remaining \\(49\\) sheep is exactly the profit.\n\nLet \\(p>0\\) be the selling price per sheep. The original cost is \\(700p\\), and the profit is \\(49p\\). Therefore the percent gain based on cost is\n\\[\n\\frac{49p}{700p}\\cdot100\\%\n=\\frac{49}{700}\\cdot100\\%\n=\\boxed{7\\%}.\n\\]\nThe answer is C.",
